   252                                  ;
   253                                  ; set up CS1# for the IDE I/O at 01F0..01FF	-- ZBIT0 disables it
   254                                  ;
   255                                  ; 7 wait states, not the 3 this carried for years.  3 was never measured;
   256                                  ; 7 was, from the monitor -- C007 written into CS1ADL by hand, then a full
   257                                  ; pass of IDENT, LBA and SECTEST against the card with no change in
   258                                  ; behaviour except that it stopped being marginal.  It matches what CS0
   259                                  ; already uses for the ECB I/O window, and the IDE path is nowhere near
   260                                  ; fast enough for four extra wait states per byte to matter: the transfer
   261                                  ; is 8-bit PIO through a single port either way.
   262                                  	winit	CS1ADH, (0x1F0 >> 6) & 0xFFFF
   137 00000134 0AF4                <1>  dw %1
   138 00000136 0700                <1>  dw %2
